  message: "Fixed in PR #4255 (origin/dev 1dd2d3ce2d), emission-parity F4 / Approach A2.\n\nBEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (full-pipeline re-probe of the filed repro): a TS file with 'import { LitElement } from \"lit\"; export class MyEl extends LitElement {}' previously emitted ZERO extends edges; it now emits 'extends typescript:lit:0-0:LitElement:unresolved' (is_resolved=False, dst_ref=ExternalRef(lit, LitElement)). 'implements OnInit' (Angular, external interface) emits a correctly-typed 'implements' edge (not mislabeled extends). Intra-repo bases still resolve to real symbols; the core inheritance-linker dedups so no duplicate edges (verified end-to-end).\n\nMECHANISM: when a class base resolves to neither a project class nor interface, _extract_inheritance_edges mints an unresolved-external edge mirroring the unresolved-CALL convention. Edge type from the implements-clause origin (_extract_implements_names); module hint from named_imports -> namespace_imports -> dotted-qualifier; aliased imports re-resolved on canonical name (local alias no longer mislabeled external); relative-imported-but-unextracted bases dropped (not mislabeled); _normalize_import_module_hint hardened against URL/Deno colon corruption. An adversarial review workflow caught the aliased-local correctness bug + the default/namespace module-hint gaps pre-merge.\n\nawaits_bakeoff_validation: this adds inheritance edges across the JS/TS corpus (affects type-hierarchy linker / centrality / framework detection via base classes); a DEEP cycle should confirm improved inheritance-graph completeness without spurious edges. SCOPE: JS/TS only; py/kotlin/ruby + core-linker chokepoint + TS interface-extends-interface tracked separately (WI-jubag + new sibling)."  # e50a
